# netsurf: Vita text with FreeType and bundled fonts (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# Hardware run 3 (doc 10): the system PGF font, rasterised once and scaled
# by vita2d, left atlas-bleed marks; Greek and Cyrillic came from the
# Japanese font at full width; Hangul, emoji and simplified Chinese were
# missing; and layout measured with other metrics than drawing used.
# - text.c/text.h (new): one FreeType engine measures and draws. Faces open
#   lazily from app0:/res/fonts/: DejaVu Sans/Serif/Mono with real bold and
#   italic faces, falling back per code point to DroidSansFallbackFull
#   (kana, CJK) and NanumGothic (Hangul). Glyphs are rasterised at the exact
#   pixel size and drawn unscaled, point-sampled, from 512x512 8-bit alpha
#   atlas pages with a 1-pixel empty gap. A full atlas drops glyphs for the
#   rest of the frame and is reset at the next frame start, after
#   sceGxmFinish, never overwritten while the GPU may read it.
# - layout.c: widths, splits and positions from the same advances as drawn.
# - plot.c: text through the engine (weight >= 600 bold, italic/oblique,
#   serif/monospace families); PGF removed. CPU clipping unchanged.
# - main.c: vita_text_frame_begin() before each frame; HUD/overlay text.
# - diag.c: face resolution for probe code points, metrics, atlas counters.
# - Makefile: text.c; freetype2 cflags. The fonts are fetched and bundled by
#   the VitaBrowser repo (tools/fetch-fonts.sh, tools/build-vita.sh).
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 5.

